From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:53:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: Keep both microphone channels on Xiaomi
 Diting

The back end fixup let TX codec DMA ports fall back to one channel, so
TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3 ran mono even with two microphones enabled. The voice
call's dual-mic noise suppression (Fluence endfire, VCPM TX channel
info 2) then got the wrong input. On Diting keep the port at the front
end's two channels (AMIC1 + AMIC5).

Local bring-up patch, not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index d8ac47422..4c25af22f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6afe.h>
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <sound/soc.h>
 #include <sound/soc-dapm.h>
@@ -128,7 +129,15 @@ static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_0:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_1:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_2:
+		channels->min = 1;
+		break;
+	/*
+	 * Two microphones (e.g. Xiaomi Diting AMIC1 + AMIC5): keep both
+	 * channels, the voice call's dual-mic noise suppression needs them.
+	 */
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3:
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,diting"))
+			break;
 		channels->min = 1;
 		break;
 	default:
